dxmt: Say in the log how busy the GPU was.

Whether a slow stretch of a game is the GPU's or the game's own could not be read from the
log: DXMT timed its waits for the GPU, not the GPU. Metal says for each command buffer when
the GPU started and when it ended it. The thread that waits for the buffers to complete sees
them in the order they were committed, and now adds up the union of those times. A swap chain
says with its other lines, every half minute and when it goes, what share of the time the GPU
was busy with the device's command buffers, what that is for a frame, and how many command
buffers a frame had:

  DXGI: the GPU in the last 30 s (frame_cause_test.exe, 14:50:39): busy 30.02 s of 30.02 s
  (100%), 44.48 ms a frame, 1.0 command buffers a frame

Checked with macos/tests/frame_cause_test.c, whose pixel shader loops a given number of times,
in a window of 1280x720 behind a locked screen (120 Hz): 0.13 ms a frame (2%) with a loop of
1; with the GPU as the limit (no display sync), 22.25 ms a frame for a loop of 4096 and 44.48
ms for one of 8192, each 100% busy and each the frame time the swap chain measures; and 4.0
command buffers a frame with three Flush() calls in a frame. Paced by the display, a loop of
64 takes 1.66 ms a frame at 20% busy, about four and a half times what a round of the loop
takes when the GPU is the limit: the GPU slows down when it has little to do. So "ms a frame"
is the GPU's time at the speed it chose, not the size of the work.

It costs two more calls into winemetal for a command buffer (GPUStartTime, which had no
wrapper, and GPUEndTime). The time is that of this device's command buffers alone: what
other processes do on the GPU is not in it. Counted from the swap chain's first frame.

LOCAL TO THIS PORT, NOT FOR DXMT. Applied by macos/build-dxmt.sh to
github.com/athei/dxmt at 01e59e9bde030f105937f249afaac92ada01b4d7, after 0001 to 0013.
Written with an AI assistant (Claude). DXMT does not accept contributions made or
co-authored by AI (its CONTRIBUTING.md), so this patch must not be sent to it as a pull
request.
---
diff --git a/src/d3d11/d3d11_swapchain.cpp b/src/d3d11/d3d11_swapchain.cpp
--- a/src/d3d11/d3d11_swapchain.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d11/d3d11_swapchain.cpp
@@ -300,6 +300,7 @@ public:
     const std::string head = Head();
     SayFrameTimes(head);
     SayCompiles(head);
+    SayGpu(head, frame_clock::now());
     // First, so that Alt+Enter no longer reaches this swap chain
     Com<IMTLDXGIFactoryPrivate> factory_private;
     if (SUCCEEDED(factory_->QueryInterface(IID_PPV_ARGS(&factory_private))))
@@ -1414,8 +1415,14 @@ private:
       if (ms > frame_worst_ms_)
         frame_worst_ms_ = ms;
     }
-    if (frame_said_ == frame_clock::time_point{})
+    if (frame_said_ == frame_clock::time_point{}) {
       frame_said_ = now;
+      // the GPU's line counts from the first frame too, not what was drawn before it
+      auto &gpu = device_->GetDXMTDevice().queue().gpu_time;
+      gpu_said_ = now;
+      gpu_said_busy_ns_ = gpu.busy_ns.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+      gpu_said_buffers_ = gpu.command_buffers.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+    }
     frame_last_ = now;
     if (now - frame_said_ >= std::chrono::seconds(30)) {
       frame_said_ = now;
@@ -1424,6 +1431,7 @@ private:
       SayWindow(head);
       SayWaits(head);
       SayCompiles(head);
+      SayGpu(head, now);
       window_frames_ = 0;
       window_slow_count_ = 0;
     }
@@ -1565,6 +1573,35 @@ private:
     said.wait_ns = wait_ns;
   }
 
+  // How busy the GPU was with this device's command buffers since the line before, from the
+  // command queue's sums: the share of the time, and what a frame took of it
+  uint64_t gpu_said_busy_ns_ = 0, gpu_said_buffers_ = 0, gpu_said_frames_ = 0;
+  frame_clock::time_point gpu_said_{};
+
+  void SayGpu(const std::string &head, frame_clock::time_point now) {
+    auto &gpu = device_->GetDXMTDevice().queue().gpu_time;
+    uint64_t busy_ns = gpu.busy_ns.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+    uint64_t buffers = gpu.command_buffers.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+    uint64_t frames = frame_count_ - gpu_said_frames_;
+    if (gpu_said_ == frame_clock::time_point{})
+      return; // no frame yet
+    double seconds = std::chrono::duration<double>(now - gpu_said_).count();
+    double busy = double(busy_ns - gpu_said_busy_ns_) / 1e9;
+    if (frames && seconds > 0) {
+      char text[512];
+      snprintf(text, sizeof(text),
+               "DXGI: the GPU in the last %.0f s%s: busy %.2f s of %.2f s (%.0f%%), %.2f ms a frame, %.1f command "
+               "buffers a frame",
+               seconds, head.c_str(), busy, seconds, 100.0 * busy / seconds, 1000.0 * busy / double(frames),
+               double(buffers - gpu_said_buffers_) / double(frames));
+      Logger::info(text);
+    }
+    gpu_said_ = now;
+    gpu_said_busy_ns_ = busy_ns;
+    gpu_said_buffers_ = buffers;
+    gpu_said_frames_ = frame_count_;
+  }
+
   void SayWindow(const std::string &head) const {
     char text[1000]; /* with "info:  " and the newline, under Wine's 1020 bytes a line */
     int used = snprintf(text, sizeof(text), "DXGI: the last 30 s%s: %llu frames, %llu over 50 ms", head.c_str(),
diff --git a/src/dxmt/dxmt_command_queue.cpp b/src/dxmt/dxmt_command_queue.cpp
--- a/src/dxmt/dxmt_command_queue.cpp
+++ b/src/dxmt/dxmt_command_queue.cpp
@@ -189,6 +189,7 @@ CommandQueue::WaitForFinishThread() {
   env::setThreadName("dxmt-finish-thread");
   SetThreadPriority(GetCurrentThread(), THREAD_PRIORITY_TIME_CRITICAL);
   uint64_t internal_seq = 1;
+  uint64_t gpu_last_end = 0;
   while (!stopped.load()) {
     ready_for_commit.wait(internal_seq, std::memory_order_acquire);
     if (stopped.load())
@@ -197,6 +198,17 @@ CommandQueue::WaitForFinishThread() {
     if (chunk.attached_cmdbuf.status() <= WMTCommandBufferStatusScheduled) {
       chunk.attached_cmdbuf.waitUntilCompleted();
     }
+    // the part of this buffer's time on the GPU that no buffer before it has counted
+    {
+      uint64_t gpu_start = chunk.attached_cmdbuf.gpuStartTime(), gpu_end = chunk.attached_cmdbuf.gpuEndTime();
+      if (gpu_end > gpu_start) {
+        if (gpu_end > gpu_last_end) {
+          gpu_time.busy_ns.fetch_add(gpu_end - std::max(gpu_start, gpu_last_end), std::memory_order_relaxed);
+          gpu_last_end = gpu_end;
+        }
+        gpu_time.command_buffers.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+      }
+    }
     if (chunk.attached_cmdbuf.status() == WMTCommandBufferStatusError) {
       ERR("Device error at frame ", chunk.frame_, ": ", chunk.attached_cmdbuf.error().description().getUTF8String());
     }
